        <p class="profile-detail-region">Battle · Europe</p>
        <h1 class="profile-detail-name">Battle of Grunwald</h1>
        <div class="info-stats" style="margin-top:10px;">
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Date</span><span class="info-stat-val">15 July 1410</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Place</span><span class="info-stat-val">Between the villages of Grünfelde (Grunwald), Tannenberg (Stębark) and Ludwigsdorf (Łodwigowo) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>'s territory, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a>; excavations of 2014 to 2019 placed the main battlefield about 2 kilometres south-west of the traditional site, south of Grunwald</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">The two sides</span><span class="info-stat-val">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-poland">Kingdom of Poland</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grand-duchy-of-lithuania">Grand Duchy of Lithuania</a> under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/w-adys-aw-ii-jagie-o">Władysław II Jagiełło</a> and Grand Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vytautas-the-great">Vytautas</a>, against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a> under Grand Master <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulrich-von-jungingen">Ulrich von Jungingen</a>; the contemporary sources give no reliable troop counts, and the high-end estimates of Stefan Kuczyński, 39,000 Polish and Lithuanian and 27,000 Teutonic men, are often cited in Western literature as commonly accepted</span></div>
          <div class="info-stat"><span class="info-stat-label">Outcome</span><span class="info-stat-val">The Teutonic army was defeated and Grand Master von <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ulrich-von-jungingen">Jungingen</a> was killed, with much of the Order's leadership. The Order held out at Marienburg and lost little land in the Peace of Thorn of 1411, but it never recovered its former power.</span></div>
        </div>
